 "notes": "Official model/model_lstm.py::ResNetLSTMSeqNet built from config/default.yaml merged with config/resnet_lstm.yaml (imu_freq=100, window_time=1.0 -> 100 samples per sub-window, seq_len=10, lstm_size=256, 1 layer, unidirectional, output_dim=3). Official input tensor is (B, 10, 6, 100) with channels [gyro_xyz, acc_xyz] in the gravity-aligned world frame with gravity removed. forward(x) returns (mean, logstd), each (B, 10, 3); forward(x, 'dp') returns mean only. The benchmark adapter feeds (B, 6, 2000) @ 200 Hz, decimates by 2 and splits into 10 x 100, so the architecture and parameter count are identical to the official configuration. param_shapes include output_block2 (covariance head) (132355 params) which receives no gradient under the official default config.",
